#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128880 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c28b8ae-71ef-5d26-895a-5d949fc5b164" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Components of the Real and Imaginary Parts of a Complex Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "6bba4758-678a-5bf6-b9df-cdc2662ab306" :question/math-academy-id "e-5525" :question/problem "If $\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}e & f \\\\ g & h\\end{bmatrix}$ are the real and imaginary parts of the matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}2 - 3\\textrm{i} & -5 - 7\\textrm{i} \\\\ 1 - 6\\textrm{i} & 5 - 9\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of $ad+eh$?" :question/worked-solution "For the given matrix $A$, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\begin{bmatrix}2 - 3\\textrm{i} & -5 - 7\\textrm{i} \\\\ 1 - 6\\textrm{i} & 5 - 9\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}_(⏟)_(Re(A)) + \\textrm{i}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -7 \\\\ -6 & -9\\end{bmatrix}_(⏟)_(Im(A))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\na=2,d=5,e=-3\n$$\n\nand $h=-9$. Therefore,\n\n$$\nad+eh=2 \\cdot 5 + (-3) \\cdot (-9) = 37\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128881 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef2e7753-83f4-5826-a04f-89616d34c578" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations to a Complex Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "0f32e78f-a13d-5e81-ba64-bff28a61aacf" :question/math-academy-id "e-5526" :question/problem "Given the matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}\\textrm{i} & -\\textrm{i} \\\\ 2 + 2\\textrm{i} & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ find the result of applying to $A$ the following elementary row operations:\n$R_1:= \\dfrac{1}{\\textrm{i}}R_1, \\qquad R_2:= R_2 - 2\\textrm{i}R_1$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the row operations to $A$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\begin{bmatrix}\\textrm{i} & -\\textrm{i} \\\\ 2 + 2\\textrm{i} & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}R_{1}:=\\frac{1}{\\textrm{i}}R_{1} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 + 2\\textrm{i} & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{vmatrix}R_{2}:=R_{2} - 2\\textrm{i}R_{1} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 + 2\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the result is\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 + 2\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128909 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83fad21d-6b36-5198-a13f-362d34342475" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying Complex Matrices"}] :question/id #uuid "27f2c303-b9a9-5337-bcea-865a9273b35b" :question/math-academy-id "e-5902" :question/problem "If $\\begin{bmatrix}-\\textrm{i} & \\textrm{i} \\\\ 1 & 2\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}1 + 2\\textrm{i} & 1 - \\textrm{i} \\\\ \\textrm{i} & 2\\end{bmatrix}$, then what is $AB$?" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the matrices using the usual method, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\begin{bmatrix}-\\textrm{i} & \\textrm{i} \\\\ 1 & 2\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 + 2\\textrm{i} & 1 - \\textrm{i} \\\\ \\textrm{i} & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}(-\\textrm{i}) \\cdot (1 + 2\\textrm{i}) + \\textrm{i} \\cdot \\textrm{i} & (-\\textrm{i}) \\cdot (1 - \\textrm{i}) + \\textrm{i} \\cdot 2 \\\\ 1 \\cdot (1 + 2\\textrm{i}) + 2\\textrm{i} \\cdot \\textrm{i} & 1 \\cdot (1 - \\textrm{i}) + 2\\textrm{i} \\cdot 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}(2 - \\textrm{i}) + (-1) & (-1 - \\textrm{i}) + 2\\textrm{i} \\\\ (1 + 2\\textrm{i}) + (-2) & (1 - \\textrm{i}) + 4\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 - \\textrm{i} & -1 + \\textrm{i} \\\\ -1 + 2\\textrm{i} & 1 + 3\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128910 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c7c1b7ad-e4bf-55b2-8665-2cf35e402946" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Complex Conjugate of a Complex Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "e8bc731b-bb0b-5a07-89d9-6acc9beebc82" :question/math-academy-id "e-5903" :question/problem "Find $B=\\overline{A}$, where $\\begin{bmatrix}4\\textrm{i} & 3 - \\textrm{i} & 1 + \\textrm{i} \\\\ 2 - 2\\textrm{i} & 2 - \\textrm{i} & 1 + 2\\textrm{i} \\\\ \\textrm{i} & 3\\textrm{i} & 2\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}$ What is the value of $b_{11} + b_{23}$?" :question/worked-solution "Taking the complex conjugate of each entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA^(―) &= \\begin{bmatrix}4\\textrm{i} & 3 - \\textrm{i} & 1 + \\textrm{i} \\\\ 2 - 2\\textrm{i} & 2 - \\textrm{i} & 1 + 2\\textrm{i} \\\\ \\textrm{i} & 3\\textrm{i} & 2\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}^(―) \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}4\\textrm{i}^(―) & 3 - \\textrm{i}^(―) & 1 + \\textrm{i}^(―) \\\\ 2 - 2\\textrm{i}^(―) & 2 - \\textrm{i}^(―) & 1 + 2\\textrm{i}^(―) \\\\ \\textrm{i}^(―) & 3\\textrm{i}^(―) & 2\\textrm{i}^(―)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-4\\textrm{i} & 3 + \\textrm{i} & 1 - \\textrm{i} \\\\ 2 + 2\\textrm{i} & 2 + \\textrm{i} & 1 - 2\\textrm{i} \\\\ -\\textrm{i} & -3\\textrm{i} & -2\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nb_{11} + b_{23} = (-4\\textrm{i}) + (1-2\\textrm{i}) = 1-6\\textrm{i}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129584 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83fad21d-6b36-5198-a13f-362d34342475" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying Complex Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c5d8ed4-6f75-5082-b7b7-e39a54276598" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}39 - 9\\textrm{i} \\\\ 12 - 9\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127299} {:answer/id #uuid "16f557a6-39d9-5b39-a9aa-ab154dca7263" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 - 9\\textrm{i} \\\\ 12 - 39\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127300} {:answer/id #uuid "578b04be-f905-5c8b-8f9f-283e54851964" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 - 9\\textrm{i} \\\\ 9 - 39\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127301} {:answer/id #uuid "5b983f8a-6bbe-5556-ae72-b3